  "summary": "Claire Lomas, a charity campaigner who gained fame for completing a marathon in a bionic suit after becoming paralyzed in a riding accident, has died at age 44. Lomas raised nearly £1m through her participation in various events. Her family announced her passing on August 22, 2023, following an accident in Jordan. In 2007, Lomas was paralyzed from the chest down after a fall during the Osberton Horse Trials. Notably, she completed the 2012 London Marathon in 17 days using a bionic suit and lit the Paralympic cauldron in Trafalgar Square that same year. In 2016, while pregnant, she completed the Great North Run over five days."
